### Consume S3 getObject stream in AWS SDK JSv3

Source: https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-js-v3/blob/main/UPGRADING.md

In JSv3, GetObject returns an unconsumed stream on the Body property. In Node.js, consume the stream using transformToString() or another consumer to free sockets and prevent connection exhaustion.

```typescript
// v3, consume the stream to free the socket.
const get = await s3.getObject({ ... }); // object .Body has unconsumed stream.
const str = await get.Body.transformToString(); // consumes the stream.
// other ways to consume the stream include writing it to a file,
// passing it to another consumer like an upload, or buffering to
// a string or byte array.
```
